CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ explicitly instantiated: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ extern template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
N5008 [temp.explicit]/12: `extern template int box<int>::put(short);'
suppresses only the implicit instantiation; the program's explicit
instantiation definition defines the same specialization.  The parser
kept such a declaration of a member function, which became a bodiless
member hiding the template ("no body for callee box<int>::put", bin53);
like a free function's, it is now discarded.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
